<body>
  <Header />
  <main>
  <article class="container">
    <header class="article-header">
      <span class="tag">PDF Tools</span>
      <h1>Smallpdf vs iLovePDF: Which PDF Editor Is Better in 2026?</h1>
      <p class="meta">Updated July 2026</p>
    </header>

    <p class="lead">
      Smallpdf and iLovePDF are the two online PDF editors most often shortlisted by users who need to compress, convert, merge, or edit PDFs without installing desktop software in 2026. Smallpdf wins on interface polish, ISO-certified security, and ease of use. iLovePDF wins on feature depth, compression quality, platform coverage, and price. This comparison breaks down features, compression, conversion, security, pricing, and ease of use so you can pick the right PDF editor for your workflow.
    </p>

    <div class="cta-top">
      <a href="https://smallpdf.com" class="btn btn-primary" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Try Smallpdf</a>
      <a href="https://www.ilovepdf.com" class="btn btn-secondary" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Try iLovePDF</a>
    </div>

    <h2>Quick Comparison</h2>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <tr><th>Feature</th><th>Smallpdf</th><th>iLovePDF</th></tr>
        <tr><td>Best For</td><td>Simple workflows, polished UX, enterprise security</td><td>Power users, compression, platform coverage, value</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Free Tier</td><td>2 tasks per day</td><td>Unlimited with ads</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Pro Price</td><td>$12/mo (annual)</td><td>$7/mo (annual)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Platforms</td><td>Web, iOS, Android</td><td>Web, iOS, Android, Windows, macOS</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Compression Levels</td><td>Basic</td><td>3 levels (basic, recommended, extreme)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>OCR</td><td>Yes (Pro)</td><td>Yes (Pro, 30+ languages)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Conversion</td><td>PDF to Office, Office to PDF</td><td>PDF to Office, Office to PDF, CAD to PDF</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Merge and Split</td><td>Yes</td><td>Yes with page reordering</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Edit PDF Text</td><td>Yes (Pro)</td><td>Yes (Pro)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Security Certifications</td><td>GDPR, ISO 27001</td><td>GDPR</td></tr>
        <tr><td>File Deletion</td><td>Within 1 hour</td><td>Within 1 hour</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Desktop App</td><td>No</td><td>Yes (Windows, macOS)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>API Access</td><td>Yes (Business)</td><td>Yes (Business)</td></tr>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>What Is Smallpdf?</h2>
    <p>Smallpdf is an online PDF editor founded in 2013 and based in Zurich, Switzerland. Smallpdf positioned itself as the simple, design-forward alternative to clunky desktop PDF software, and its clean interface and focused toolset made it one of the most popular PDF tools on the web. By 2026, Smallpdf serves more than 100 million users and offers a Pro subscription with unlimited tasks, OCR, and advanced editing features.</p>
    <p>The defining characteristic of Smallpdf is its interface. Each PDF task is a single, focused tool: Compress PDF, Convert PDF, Merge PDF, Split PDF, Edit PDF, and so on. You drag your file onto the tool, Smallpdf processes it, and you download the result. This simplicity makes Smallpdf the easiest PDF editor to use, especially for users who only need one task at a time. The trade-off is that Smallpdf offers fewer features per tool than iLovePDF, and its free tier limits you to 2 tasks per day.</p>

    <h2>What Is iLovePDF?</h2>
    <p>iLovePDF is an online PDF editor founded in 2010 and based in Barcelona, Spain. iLovePDF positioned itself as the comprehensive, free alternative to paid PDF software, offering unlimited free use with ads and a Pro subscription that removes ads and adds advanced features. By 2026, iLovePDF serves more than 200 million users and offers desktop apps for Windows and macOS alongside its web and mobile apps.</p>
    <p>The defining characteristic of iLovePDF is its feature depth. Each PDF tool offers more options than Smallpdf: compression has three levels, merge lets you reorder pages, conversion supports more formats including CAD, and OCR supports over 30 languages. iLovePDF also offers desktop apps, which means you can process PDFs offline without uploading files to the cloud. The trade-off is a slightly less polished interface and ads on the free tier, though the Pro plan removes both.</p>

    <h2>Feature Depth and Tool Variety</h2>
    <p>Feature depth is where iLovePDF establishes a clear lead. Smallpdf offers a cleaner, more focused toolset, while iLovePDF offers more options per tool and supports more formats.</p>

    <h3>iLovePDF More Options Per Tool</h3>
    <p>iLovePDF's tools offer more granularity than Smallpdf's. The compression tool has three levels (basic, recommended, extreme), letting you balance file size against quality. The merge tool lets you reorder pages and extract specific page ranges. The conversion tool supports PDF to Word, Excel, PowerPoint, and also CAD to PDF, which Smallpdf does not offer. For users who need fine control over their PDF tasks, iLovePDF is the stronger choice.</p>

    <h3>Smallpdf Focused Simplicity</h3>
    <p>Smallpdf's tools are simpler but more focused. Each tool does one thing well, with minimal options to configure. This makes Smallpdf easier to use for users who just want a quick result, but it limits users who need more control. For example, Smallpdf's compression tool has a single level, and its merge tool does not support page reordering. For simple workflows, Smallpdf is sufficient; for complex workflows, iLovePDF is more capable.</p>
    <p><strong>Winner:</strong> Best feature depth and tool variety goes to <span class="winner-tag">iLovePDF</span>.</p>

    <h2>Compression Quality and Performance</h2>
    <p>Compression is one of the most common PDF tasks, and iLovePDF has a measurable edge in compression quality and flexibility.</p>

    <h3>iLovePDF Three Compression Levels</h3>
    <p>iLovePDF offers three compression levels: basic (slight reduction, high quality), recommended (balanced), and extreme (maximum reduction, lower quality). This lets you choose the right trade-off for your use case, whether you are emailing a document, uploading it to a web form with a size limit, or archiving it. In testing, iLovePDF's extreme compression produces smaller files than Smallpdf's single-level compression, with acceptable quality for most uses.</p>

    <h3>Smallpdf Single-Level Compression</h3>
    <p>Smallpdf offers a single compression level that produces good results but without the flexibility of iLovePDF's three levels. For users who need maximum compression to fit a file under a size limit, Smallpdf may not go far enough, forcing a second pass with another tool. For users who just want a quick, good-enough compression, Smallpdf is fine.</p>
    <p><strong>Winner:</strong> Best compression quality and flexibility goes to <span class="winner-tag">iLovePDF</span>.</p>

    <h2>Conversion and Format Support</h2>
    <p>Both tools convert between PDF and Office formats, but iLovePDF supports more formats, including CAD and image formats.</p>

    <h3>iLovePDF Broader Format Support</h3>
    <p>iLovePDF converts PDF to Word, Excel, PowerPoint, JPG, and back, plus CAD to PDF, which is valuable for architects and engineers. It also supports HTML to PDF, PDF to PDF/A for archiving, and PDF to ePub for ebooks. For users who work with a variety of document formats, iLovePDF's broader format support is a meaningful advantage.</p>

    <h3>Smallpdf Core Conversion</h3>
    <p>Smallpdf covers the core conversions: PDF to Word, Excel, PowerPoint, JPG, and back. It also supports PDF to PDF/A. However, it does not support CAD to PDF, HTML to PDF, or PDF to ePub. For users who only need Office format conversions, Smallpdf is sufficient; for users who need broader format support, iLovePDF is the better choice.</p>
    <p><strong>Winner:</strong> Best conversion and format support goes to <span class="winner-tag">iLovePDF</span>.</p>

    <h2>Security and Privacy</h2>
    <p>Both tools take security seriously, but Smallpdf has stronger certifications, which matters for enterprise users.</p>

    <h3>Smallpdf ISO 27001 Certified</h3>
    <p>Smallpdf is GDPR compliant and ISO 27001 certified, which is a formal information security management standard. This certification matters for enterprise buyers who require vendors to meet specific security standards. Smallpdf also deletes uploaded files within 1 hour of processing, and its servers are located in the EU, which simplifies GDPR compliance for European users.</p>

    <h3>iLovePDF GDPR Compliant</h3>
    <p>iLovePDF is GDPR compliant and deletes uploaded files within 1 hour of processing. It uses SSL encryption for file transfers and stores files on secure servers. However, iLovePDF does not hold ISO 27001 certification, which may matter for enterprise buyers with strict vendor security requirements. For most users, iLovePDF's security is adequate; for enterprises with formal security requirements, Smallpdf's certifications are a differentiator.</p>
    <p><strong>Winner:</strong> Best security certifications goes to <span class="winner-tag">Smallpdf</span>. For everyday use, both are secure.</p>

    <h2>Platform Coverage and Offline Use</h2>
    <p>iLovePDF offers broader platform coverage, including desktop apps for Windows and macOS, which Smallpdf does not.</p>

    <h3>iLovePDF Desktop Apps</h3>
    <p>iLovePDF offers desktop apps for Windows and macOS, which let you process PDFs offline without uploading files to the cloud. This matters for users who work with sensitive documents that cannot leave their machine, or for users in areas with unreliable internet. The desktop apps include the same tools as the web version and are included with the Pro subscription.</p>

    <h3>Smallpdf Web and Mobile Only</h3>
    <p>Smallpdf is available on web, iOS, and Android, but does not offer a desktop app. All processing happens in the cloud, which means you need an internet connection and must upload files to Smallpdf's servers. For users who need offline processing or who cannot upload sensitive files, Smallpdf is a limitation.</p>
    <p><strong>Winner:</strong> Best platform coverage and offline use goes to <span class="winner-tag">iLovePDF</span>.</p>

    <h2>Pricing Comparison</h2>
    <p>Pricing is one of the biggest differentiators. iLovePDF is significantly more affordable than Smallpdf, especially on annual plans.</p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <tr><th>Tier</th><th>Smallpdf</th><th>iLovePDF</th></tr>
        <tr><td>Free</td><td>2 tasks per day</td><td>Unlimited with ads</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Pro (monthly)</td><td>$12/mo</td><td>$9/mo</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Pro (annual)</td><td>$12/mo (billed annually)</td><td>$7/mo (billed annually)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Team</td><td>$10/user/mo (annual)</td><td>$6/user/mo (annual)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>OCR</td><td>Pro and up</td><td>Pro and up</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Desktop App</td><td>Not available</td><td>Included with Pro</td></tr>
        <tr><td>API Access</td><td>Business plan</td><td>Business plan</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Ad-Free</td><td>Pro and up</td><td>Pro and up</td></tr>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>iLovePDF is the clear value winner. At $7 per month on the annual plan, iLovePDF Pro costs nearly half of Smallpdf Pro's $12 per month, while including more features (desktop apps, more compression levels, broader format support). For budget-conscious users, iLovePDF is the smarter financial choice.</p>
    <p>Smallpdf's higher price buys a more polished interface and ISO 27001 security certification, which may justify the premium for enterprise buyers. For most individual users and small teams, however, iLovePDF delivers more value for less money.</p>
    <p><strong>Winner:</strong> Best pricing and value goes to <span class="winner-tag">iLovePDF</span>.</p>

    <h2>Pros and Cons</h2>

    <h3>Smallpdf Pros</h3>
    <div class="pros-box">
      <ul>
        <li>Polished, design-forward interface is the easiest to use</li>
        <li>ISO 27001 certified and GDPR compliant for enterprise security</li>
        <li>Servers located in the EU for GDPR simplicity</li>
        <li>Focused toolset makes simple tasks fast</li>
        <li>Mobile apps for iOS and Android</li>
        <li>API access for business integrations</li>
        <li>Files deleted within 1 hour for privacy</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h3>Smallpdf Cons</h3>
    <div class="cons-box">
      <ul>
        <li>Free tier limited to 2 tasks per day</li>
        <li>Pro at $12/mo is nearly double iLovePDF's price</li>
        <li>No desktop app, all processing is cloud-based</li>
        <li>Fewer options per tool than iLovePDF</li>
        <li>Single compression level limits flexibility</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h3>iLovePDF Pros</h3>
    <div class="pros-box">
      <ul>
        <li>Unlimited free tier (with ads) for everyday use</li>
        <li>Pro at $7/mo is the best value in the category</li>
        <li>Desktop apps for Windows and macOS included</li>
        <li>Three compression levels for flexibility</li>
        <li>Broader format support including CAD and ePub</li>
        <li>OCR in 30+ languages</li>
        <li>Page reordering in merge tool</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h3>iLovePDF Cons</h3>
    <div class="cons-box">
      <ul>
        <li>Free tier shows ads, which can be distracting</li>
        <li>Interface is less polished than Smallpdf</li>
        <li>No ISO 27001 certification, only GDPR compliance</li>
        <li>More options can overwhelm simple users</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h2>Who Should Use Which?</h2>

    <div class="use-case">
      <h3>Users Who Want the Easiest Tool</h3>
      <p>If you want the simplest, most polished PDF editing experience and do not mind paying a premium, Smallpdf is the better choice. Its focused toolset and clean interface make it the easiest PDF editor to use, especially for users who only need one task at a time and want a polished experience.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="use-case">
      <h3>Budget-Conscious Power Users</h3>
      <p>If you want the most features for the lowest price, iLovePDF is the better choice. At $7 per month on the annual plan, iLovePDF Pro includes more features than Smallpdf Pro at nearly half the price, making it the clear value winner for users who need compression, conversion, OCR, and desktop apps.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="use-case">
      <h3>Enterprise Security Buyers</h3>
      <p>If your organization requires ISO 27001 certification for vendor security, Smallpdf is the better choice. Its ISO 27001 certification and EU-based servers simplify enterprise security reviews and GDPR compliance. iLovePDF is GDPR compliant but lacks the ISO certification that some enterprises require.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="use-case">
      <h3>Users Who Need Offline Processing</h3>
      <p>If you need to process PDFs offline without uploading files to the cloud, iLovePDF is the better choice. Its desktop apps for Windows and macOS let you process PDFs locally, which matters for sensitive documents or areas with unreliable internet. Smallpdf is cloud-only and cannot process files offline.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="use-case">
      <h3>Users Who Work with CAD Files</h3>
      <p>If you work with CAD files and need to convert them to PDF, iLovePDF is the better choice. It supports CAD to PDF conversion, which Smallpdf does not. For architects, engineers, and designers who regularly work with CAD files, iLovePDF's broader format support is a decisive advantage.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Real-World Use Cases</h2>

    <div class="use-case">
      <h3>Compressing a large PDF for email</h3>
      <p>A user needs to compress a 50 MB PDF to under 10 MB to email it. iLovePDF's extreme compression level reduces the file to 8 MB with acceptable quality, while Smallpdf's single-level compression only reduces it to 15 MB, which exceeds the email limit. The user runs a second pass with another tool to get under 10 MB, which would not be necessary with iLovePDF's extreme level.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="use-case">
      <h3>Merging multiple PDFs with page reordering</h3>
      <p>A project manager needs to merge five PDF reports into one document and reorder some pages. iLovePDF's merge tool lets the manager drag and drop pages to reorder them before merging, producing a single, organized document. Smallpdf's merge tool combines the files in upload order without reordering, forcing the manager to use a separate tool to rearrange pages.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="use-case">
      <h3>Processing sensitive legal documents offline</h3>
      <p>A law firm needs to compress and merge sensitive legal documents without uploading them to the cloud. iLovePDF's desktop app for macOS lets the firm process the documents locally, keeping them on the firm's machines. Smallpdf is cloud-only and would require uploading sensitive documents to external servers, which the firm's security policy prohibits.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="use-case">
      <h3>Converting CAD files to PDF for client review</h3>
      <p>An architect needs to convert CAD drawings to PDF for client review. iLovePDF's CAD to PDF conversion handles the drawings directly, producing clean PDFs for the client. Smallpdf does not support CAD conversion, forcing the architect to use a separate CAD application to export PDFs, which adds steps to the workflow.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="use-case">
      <h3>Enterprise procurement with security requirements</h3>
      <p>A large enterprise needs a PDF editor for 500 employees and requires ISO 27001 certification for all vendors. Smallpdf's ISO 27001 certification passes the enterprise's security review, while iLovePDF's GDPR compliance alone does not meet the ISO requirement. The enterprise chooses Smallpdf despite the higher price, because the certification is non-negotiable.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Final Verdict</h2>
    <div class="verdict">
      <p><strong>Best overall for features and value: iLovePDF.</strong> iLovePDF's $7 per month Pro plan, three compression levels, broader format support, desktop apps, and OCR in 30+ languages make it the best value PDF editor in 2026. For most users who need a capable, affordable PDF tool, iLovePDF is the clear choice.</p>
      <p><strong>Best for simplicity and enterprise security: Smallpdf.</strong> Smallpdf's polished interface and ISO 27001 certification make it the best choice for users who prioritize ease of use or who work in enterprises with strict security requirements. For simple workflows and enterprise procurement, Smallpdf justifies its premium.</p>
      <p><strong>Best budget choice for occasional use: iLovePDF.</strong> iLovePDF's unlimited free tier (with ads) makes it the best choice for users who only need occasional PDF editing and do not want to pay. Smallpdf's 2-task-per-day free limit is restrictive for users who need more than a couple of tasks.</p>
      <p><strong>Recommended combo:</strong> For organizations with diverse needs, run Smallpdf for enterprise security and iLovePDF for power users and offline processing. This hybrid approach uses each tool where it is strongest and avoids forcing one tool into a use case it was not designed for.</p>
